# grammar_held.gbnf — the Executor's mask PLUS a [HELD] seat.
# PAIRED WITH contract_held.txt; they are ONE artifact and neither
# may be edited without the other.
#
# Selected only while /held is non-empty AND GT_HELD_SKIN=1.
# The original grammar.gbnf + contract.txt pair is untouched and is
# the mask used otherwise. This file is never the default.
#
# EVERY RULE IS ON ONE LINE. llama.cpp's GBNF parser does not support a rule
# continuing onto a second line and IT FAILS SILENTLY: the server returns 200
# and generates completely ungoverned prose.
#
# WHAT THIS ADDS: a required [HELD] section of one line after the answer.
# Known risk: extra structure in the same pass crushed speech on a small
# model. That is why this pair sits behind GT_HELD_SKIN=1.
#
# WHAT IS STILL DELIBERATELY ABSENT (same as grammar.gbnf):
#   NO [WHISTLEBLOWER] SECTION. Python is the clerk.
#   NO [PROXY] SECTION.
#   NO DECLARED ACTIONS TRIPLET BLOCK.
#   NO EVIDENCE LINE.

root ::= "ANSWER_START\n" executor-section held-section "ANSWER_END"
executor-section ::= "[EXECUTOR]\n" body
held-section ::= "[HELD]\n" bline
bline ::= [^\n[<] [^\n]* "\n"
body ::= bline bline? bline? bline? bline? bline? bline? bline?
